Hello everyone, thank you for Joining me for this weekly review. Not! I am
going to go over everything from this week and this last week in my next
email. For today I have a few random things from Elder Killian's brain to
share =F0=9F=A7=A0

Spiritual message/update

This past week has been great, and I've only felt anxious a couple times
and only for a few minutes at a time. There are a couple reasons I believe
this is the case.

1. Prayer

Ever since I've started experiencing these somewhat anxious feelings I've
immediately taken to the knees to pray about it to my Heavenly Father. I
trust that He hears my prayers and is concerned about my well-being. I also
believe that the Heavenly Help we are prescribed is correlated somehow to
our faith and open-ness with God. I haven't felt immediate relief from
these feelings in the moment, but steadily I have noticed a positive
change. I attribute this to Heavenly Father, and also in part to my trust
that I place in Him.

2. Anxious vs Anxiously Engaged

Doctrine and Covenants chapter 58 reads:
27 Verily I say, men should be anxiously engaged in a good cause, and do
many things of their own free will, and bring to pass much righteousness;
28 For the power is in them, wherein they are agents unto themselves. And
inasmuch as men do good they shall in nowise lose their reward.

We sometimes can't 100 percent control our emotions or our circumstances,
but there are things that we can control, as we are "agents unto
[ourselves.]" I have had an increased focus on this kind of mindset these
past couple of weeks, and it's made all the difference. As I focus on
putting all of my efforts into bringing others closer to the Savior and
showing love unto my brothers and sisters in Japan, I have slowly seen the
anxious feelings I've felt get pushed to the side, or even covered up by
the bright and rejoicable experiences I have seen through that increased
focus.

I am very grateful for what God and the Savior have done to ease my
burdens. I promise that as You (whoever you may be, member of the Church or
not) walk forward with trust that you are being watched over, and acting in
Righteousness, you will be blessed and see a great change in your lives. We
all need to change, no matter where we are at. I am still trying to change
each day, failing, repenting, and slowly crawling forward. Some days feel
like I'm being dragged backwards! But I have the desire to move forward,
and thanks to the Savior sometimes that's even enough.

Poetry

1. Never-woulda-thought

Pokemon is Lit
My companion is Brainwashed
It's pretty funny =F0=9F=98=82

2. Crime Seen

Stem cells peek around the corner;
The left side of my brain has got
The right side of my brain in a choke-hold and if I said that the left side
wasn't being bold I would be denying I'm a foreigner, which would therefore
be a lie that I'd just told. The reason there's an argument is that the
left side really meant to argue just for the sake of it, and it didn't sit
right with the right side of my brain. "It wouldn't be right" just to leave
those words suspended in the air so the right side of my brain upended the
chair of the left side (who wasn't on the right side at the time) which (if
I'm right) provoked the scene and the image that we've just imagined right
here. I've got nothing left to say 'sides this whole thing just so happened
to be a stroke of luck or a stroke of genius. On second thought it might be
right to say it was just a stroke.

3. Ceramic Feathers

If a bird of ceramic took flight
It would have to be due to a trick
With "feathers of masonry?" Yeah, right
I refuse to imagine they'd stick

In this moment just now
I realized... something grand
As I furrow my brow
In disbelief and

Close off my mind to the idea of this event
It's quite obvious now that things just won't go how I'd meant

If we limit ourselves from the get-go I fear
That aside from this "brick bird" much greater, much more important things
will veer

Off course
Astray
Into lost places
Far away

So make the decision to stretch your perspective
There's no need to scrutinize like a detective
Think openly and take all your measures
To fly far away on your ceramic feathers

Conclusion!

Thanks for tuning in. I had fun writing each part of this, and I hope it
will have some meaning with whoever reads this. Love you guys!!

Elder Killian

